{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfZNkLNik7kVRAczNuwcX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the candidate `person_prototype_representativeness` and it passes the admission self-check (`OK`). There is one risk: its ELPD-LOO estimate may be flagged as unreliable.\n\n**The change:** it refines the incumbent `local_representativeness` in one way. In the original, everyone shares one \"prototype\" alternation rate, the amount of back-and-forth a person expects a random sequence to have, and it is forced above 0.5. Here each participant gets their own prototype rate, drawn from a population distribution, and it may fall below 0.5 (people who expect streaky sequences) or above it (people who expect lots of alternation). Local balance, the periodicity penalty and the rest of the scoring stay as in the original, though I also swapped its flat priors for gentler ones.\n\n**Why:** the critique's one finding that survives the FDR correction is that people differ in how much they prefer alternation far more than a single shared rate can produce (observed 0.217 vs 0.053 expected, q = 0.016).\n\n**Self-check result:** the model loads, honours the data contract and finished the short test fit, with an ELPD-LOO of −1049.0. The incumbent's is −1398.4 from its full fit, so it looks much better, but this was one short chain, so it is only indicative.\n\n**Things to watch:**\n- **LOO may be unreliable.** In the test fit 11.2% of trials had high Pareto k, well above the 1% tolerance. That is common with one parameter per participant. If the full fit shows the same, the model's ELPD-LOO counts as unreliable and it cannot be exported as the winner even if it scores best.\n- **It won't be used in experiment design.** Because it depends on `participant_id`, the design step leaves it out. For the novelty check it is averaged over the training participants.\n- **The participant limit is hard-coded at 256.** It holds 256 per-participant slots (41 are used now). An id of 256 or higher raises an error instead of being silently merged with another participant.\n\nThe files are in `.../experiment1/model_loop/iter_0/candidate_4/`: `hypothesis.md`, `model_name.txt` and `candidate.py`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3675,"cache_read_input_tokens":56448,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3675,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7d32bf2-d4cf-4adb-bca4-4148d30a4dae","uuid":"9122f014-d5d8-4cc9-8e2a-19b54a0c3314","timestamp":"2026-09-30T09:19:47.299Z","request_id":"req_011CfZNkKoj1w1HaCyQhAn25"}
